  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Signal & Void",
    "overview": "A terminal for the AI era: signal separated from noise. The page is a deep, violet-cast void, never grey and never cream. Light shows up in it as emission rather than paint. A single plasma violet carries the brand. A cyan signal marks the technical metadata (versions, commands, live state), the way a cursor marks the active line. The editorial serif headline set against mono labels says the catalog is curated, but the goods are developer tools.\n\nDensity is moderate. Catalog grids are calm cards on a flat surface, and the atmosphere (CSS nebula, optional WebGL plasma field, faint 56px grid, grain) lives only behind the hero. Motion is short and purposeful. Nothing except the hero manifest sequence and the marquee runs longer than 640 ms, and every effect has a reduced-motion end state that renders without script.\n\nPersian (RTL) is first-class. Estedad replaces both faces, tracking and capitals are removed from joined script everywhere, and creator-supplied English inside a Persian page keeps its own direction.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Violet-cast dark void as the default theme; a hand-tuned \"Daylight Void\" light theme, not an inversion.",
      "One brand hue (Plasma 292) covering large areas; cyan Signal (196) only on small technical elements.",
      "Plasma → Ion → Signal sweep as the one signature gradient, for display text and hairline rules.",
      "Newsreader editorial serif for headings, Geist for UI, Geist Mono for uppercase eyebrows.",
      "Terminal motifs: blinking caret in the logo, typed manifest in the hero, mono metadata.",
      "Flat tonal surfaces with a hover lift; glow reserved for rare brand moments."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Plasma Coverage Rule",
        "body": "Plasma is the only colour allowed to cover large areas. Every other hue is a detail.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signal Stays Small Rule",
        "body": "Signal lives on dots, carets, version chips and info text. If a Signal shape is bigger than a button, it's wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ion Never Fills Rule",
        "body": "Ion appears only inside gradients. A flat Ion fill breaks the system.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Verified Lock Rule",
        "body": "If it's green, it's a trust claim. Green never decorates.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Joined Script Rule",
        "body": "No tracking and no capitals on Persian text, anywhere. Eyebrows are told apart by colour and size alone. Latin data islands (`dir=\"ltr\"`) keep their styling.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bidi Plaintext Rule",
        "body": "Creator-supplied text (`.ts-bidi`) takes its direction from its first strong character, so English in a Persian page keeps its full stop at the end.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Metric Fallback Rule",
        "body": "Every web font has a size-adjusted local fallback, so the swap never moves text.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Rhythm Rule",
        "body": "Sections never set their own block padding. They use `.section-y`.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Emission Rule",
        "body": "Glow means something is emitting signal. If nothing is live or branded, there's no glow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Atmosphere Stays Behind the Hero Rule",
        "body": "The nebula, plasma field, grid field and grain belong to the hero. Catalog and dashboard surfaces stay quiet.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reference colours through the theme tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`), never raw OKLCH in components, so both themes work.",
      "Do keep Plasma as the only large-area colour, and keep Signal on elements no bigger than a button.",
      "Do use `.editorial` for every heading and `.eyebrow` for every label above one.",
      "Do use `.section-y` and `.container-page` for every section.",
      "Do give every effect a reduced-motion end state that renders without script. Use durations from the token set (80–640 ms) and `--ease-out-expo` for entrances.",
      "Do use `data-enter=\"nudge\"` (rise, no fade) on the LCP text. A fade on it costs ~430 ms of mobile LCP.",
      "Do use logical properties and `rtl:` icon flips, and wrap versions, commands and dates in `dir=\"ltr\"`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use Ion as a flat fill, or green for anything that isn't a trust claim.",
      "Don't put tracking or uppercase on Persian text.",
      "Don't put the nebula, grid field or glow on catalog or dashboard surfaces.",
      "Don't cancel the focus ring with `outline-none` unless a ring replaces it.",
      "Don't set type below 11 px. The trust chip's 9 px sub-line and the stray 10 px labels are baseline drift, not precedent.",
      "Don't invent tracking values. The baseline already scatters 0.12em, 0.14em and 0.16em; the eyebrow's 0.16em is the token.",
      "Don't reach for `rounded-2xl`. It sits below `rounded-xl` in this scale."
    ]
  }
}
